# Standalone dev defaults (`npm run dev`, no AppHost) -- these match
# App.vue's own hardcoded JS-level fallbacks exactly (its own comment:
# "only applies when running client-web standalone... no AppHost at
# all"). Plain `.env` (not `.env.development`) so it loads for every Vite
# mode, including `--mode vitals`/`--mode meridian` below -- those only
# layer their own domain-specific vars on top of this file, they don't
# replace it. When run under EventStore.AppHost instead, AppHost.cs's own
# WithEnvironment calls override every one of these with the real
# Aspire-assigned values.
#
# 5001/5010 match eventstore/devidp's own pinned dev ports
# (EventStore.AppHost/AppHost.cs) -- run both directly (`dotnet run` in
# each project) for this file's own defaults to actually resolve.
#
# VITE_AUTH_BASE_URL is devIdp's HTTP endpoint (5010), not HTTPS (5011) --
# see App.vue's own comment on its matching JS-level fallback for why
# ("Forbidden -- caller's token does not hold the required scope" if the
# two ever mismatch again).
VITE_HOST_BASE_URL=https://localhost:5001
VITE_AUTH_BASE_URL=http://localhost:5010
